From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:24:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Add SM8650 MDSS compatible to client
 list

Add the SM8650 MDSS to the clients that get an identity default domain,
as the other MDSS versions do. The bootloader leaves the display
scanning out its splash, and with a DMA domain the scanout faults on
the splash addresses until the display driver takes over.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 795e8ec7e..40c35e5d7 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -426,6 +426,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8450-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
-- 
2.55.0

